Rem ==================================================================
Rem stats.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: statistics
Rem
Rem Descriptive statistics, correlation and regression, and the classic
Rem inference tests, pure Shoddy on top of the runtime's special
Rem functions (ERF, GAMMAP, BETAI — the CDF primitives that need native
Rem precision) and the SORT builtin. Every p-value is a real p-value
Rem computed from a CDF; there are no critical-value tables here.
Rem
Rem Scale: lists are linked lists and most words walk them more than
Rem once, so this is for classroom-sized data — dozens to thousands of
Rem values — not bulk analytics.
Rem
Rem Conventions:
Rem   * Var/StdDev are the SAMPLE forms (divide by n-1); VarP/StdDevP
Rem     are the population forms (divide by n).
Rem   * Quantile uses linear interpolation between order statistics —
Rem     R type 7, the same rule as Excel's PERCENTILE.INC.
Rem   * Skewness and Kurtosis are the moment (population) forms, as in
Rem     scipy with bias=True; Kurtosis is excess (normal = 0).
Rem   * Modes returns ALL modes; a tie is never silently broken.
Rem   * Test words return a TestResult(Stat, Df, PVal) record with a
Rem     two-sided p-value. Df is 0 where no df applies (z-tests); for
Rem     Anova it is the between-groups df (within = total n - groups).
Rem   * Frequency words return dict.shoddy association lists, keys in
Rem     first-seen order.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "seq.shoddy"
Include "dict.shoddy"

Rem ---- aggregation (poly) --------------------------------------------

Def Sum(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Fold(xs, 0, +)

Def Product(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Fold(xs, 1, *)

Def Maximum(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Fold(xs, First(xs), Max)

Def Minimum(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Fold(xs, First(xs), Min)

Rem ---- central tendency ----------------------------------------------

Def Mean(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Sum(xs) / Length(xs)

Rem The everyday name, kept as an alias for Mean.
Def Average(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Mean(xs)

Def WeightedMean(xs As List Of Number, ws As List Of Number) As Number
    Sum(ZipWith(xs, ws, *)) / Sum(ws)

Rem For rates, ratios, growth factors. All values must be positive.
Def GeoMean(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Exp(Mean(Map(xs, Log)))

Def HarmonicMean(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Length(xs) / Sum(Map(xs, Fn(x) => 1 / x))

Rem ---- quantiles -----------------------------------------------------

Rem Linear interpolation between order statistics (R type 7 / Excel
Rem PERCENTILE.INC): position h = (n-1)p + 1 in the sorted data, then
Rem interpolate between the values on either side. p is a fraction.
Def Quantile(xs As List Of Number, p As Number) As Number
    If p < 0 Or p > 1 Then
        Error("QUANTILE: P OUTSIDE [0, 1]")
    Else
        Let s = Sort(xs)
        Let h = (Length(s) - 1) * p + 1
        Let lo = Floor(h)
        Nth(s, lo) + (h - lo) * (Nth(s, Ceil(h)) - Nth(s, lo))

Rem The same, taking 0..100 instead of 0..1.
Def Percentile(xs As List Of Number, k As Number) As Number
    Quantile(xs, k / 100)

Def Median(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Quantile(xs, 0.5)

Def Iqr(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Quantile(xs, 0.75) - Quantile(xs, 0.25)

Rem Max - min. (Not "Range" — that word is the builtin that builds
Rem { a .. b }, and a Def would silently shadow it.)
Def RangeOf(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Maximum(xs) - Minimum(xs)

Rem ---- spread --------------------------------------------------------

Rem Two-pass sum of squared deviations: mean first, then deviations —
Rem numerically stable, and the shared core of the variance words.
Def SqDevSum(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Let m = Mean(xs)
    Sum(Map(xs, Fn(x) => (x - m) * (x - m)))

Rem Sample variance (n-1) and population variance (n).
Def Var(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    SqDevSum(xs) / (Length(xs) - 1)

Def VarP(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    SqDevSum(xs) / Length(xs)

Def StdDev(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Sqr(Var(xs))

Def StdDevP(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Sqr(VarP(xs))

Rem Standard error of the mean.
Def StdErr(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    StdDev(xs) / Sqr(Length(xs))

Rem Median absolute deviation — robust spread.
Def Mad(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Let m = Median(xs)
    Median(Map(xs, Fn(x) => Abs(x - m)))

Rem ---- shape ---------------------------------------------------------

Def Skewness(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Let m = Mean(xs)
    Let n = Length(xs)
    Let m2 = SqDevSum(xs) / n
    Sum(Map(xs, Fn(x) => (x - m) * (x - m) * (x - m))) / n / m2 ^ 1.5

Rem Excess kurtosis: 0 for the normal distribution.
Def Kurtosis(xs As List Of Number) As Number
    Let m = Mean(xs)
    Let n = Length(xs)
    Let m2 = SqDevSum(xs) / n
    Sum(Map(xs, Fn(x) => (x - m) ^ 4)) / n / (m2 * m2) - 3

Rem ---- z-scores and outliers -----------------------------------------

Def ZScore(x As Number, m As Number, s As Number) As Number
    (x - m) / s

Rem Standardize a whole dataset against its own mean and sample SD.
Def ZScores(xs As List Of Number) As List Of Number
    Let m = Mean(xs)
    Let s = StdDev(xs)
    Map(xs, Fn(x) => (x - m) / s)

Rem The 1.5 x IQR rule: values beyond the box-plot fences.
Def Outliers(xs As List Of Number) As List Of Number
    Let q1 = Quantile(xs, 0.25)
    Let q3 = Quantile(xs, 0.75)
    Let lo = q1 - 1.5 * (q3 - q1)
    Let hi = q3 + 1.5 * (q3 - q1)
    Filter(xs, Fn(x) => x < lo Or x > hi)

Rem Values more than z sample standard deviations from the mean.
Def OutliersZ(xs As List Of Number, z As Number) As List Of Number
    Let m = Mean(xs)
    Let s = StdDev(xs)
    Filter(xs, Fn(x) => Abs(x - m) / s > z)

Rem ---- frequencies (dict.shoddy association lists) ---------------------

Def FreqBump(d As List Of Pair, x As t) As List Of Pair
    If IsEmpty(d) Then
        { Pair(x, 1) }
    Else
        If Fst(First(d)) = x Then
            Prepend(Pair(x, Snd(First(d)) + 1), Rest(d))
        Else
            Prepend(First(d), FreqBump(Rest(d), x))

Rem Value -> count, keys in first-seen order. Works for any key type
Rem = accepts: numbers, strings, booleans, records.
Def Freq(xs As List Of t) As List Of Pair
    Fold(xs, { }, FreqBump)

Rem Value -> proportion of the whole (multiply by 100 for percentages).
Def RelFreq(xs As List Of t) As List Of Pair
    Let n = Length(xs)
    Map(Freq(xs), Fn(p) => Pair(Fst(p), Snd(p) / n))

Rem ALL the most frequent values, in first-seen order — a tie returns
Rem every winner, never a silent pick (if every value is unique, every
Rem value is a mode).
Def Modes(xs As List Of t) As List Of t
    Let f = Freq(xs)
    Let top = Maximum(Map(f, Snd))
    Map(Filter(f, Fn(p) => Snd(p) = top), Fst)

Rem Empirical CDF: the proportion of the data <= x.
Def Ecdf(xs As List Of Number, x As Number) As Number
    CountIf(xs, <=(x)) / Length(xs)

Rem ---- correlation and regression ---------------------------------------

Rem Sample covariance (n-1), the primitive under Correl and LinFit.
Def Cov(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Number
    Let mx = Mean(xs)
    Let my = Mean(ys)
    Sum(ZipWith(xs, ys, Fn(x, y) => (x - mx) * (y - my))) / (Length(xs) - 1)

Rem Pearson correlation coefficient, in [-1, 1].
Def Correl(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Number
    Cov(xs, ys) / (StdDev(xs) * StdDev(ys))

Rem Average rank of x within xs (ties share the mean of their ranks).
Def RankOf(xs As List Of Number, x As Number) As Number
    CountIf(xs, <(x)) + (CountIf(xs, =(x)) + 1) / 2

Def Ranks(xs As List Of Number) As List Of Number
    Map(xs, Fn(x) => RankOf(xs, x))

Rem Spearman rank correlation: Pearson on the ranks — the robust,
Rem nonparametric complement to Correl.
Def Spearman(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Number
    Correl(Ranks(xs), Ranks(ys))

Rem Simple linear regression y = Slope * x + Intercept, with R2 the
Rem share of y's variance the line explains.
Type Fit
    Slope As Number
    Intercept As Number
    R2 As Number

Def LinFit(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Fit
    Let b = Cov(xs, ys) / Var(xs)
    Let r = Correl(xs, ys)
    Fit(b, Mean(ys) - b * Mean(xs), r * r)

Rem ---- distributions ---------------------------------------------------
Rem CDFs from the runtime's special functions: normal from ERF,
Rem chi-square from GAMMAP, t and F from BETAI.

Def NormPdf(z As Number) As Number
    Exp(-(z * z) / 2) / Sqr(2 * Pi())

Rem Standard normal CDF. For general x, pass ZScore(x, mu, sigma).
Def NormCdf(z As Number) As Number
    (1 + Erf(z / Sqr(2))) / 2

Def Chi2Cdf(x As Number, df As Number) As Number
    GammaP(df / 2, x / 2)

Def TCdf(t As Number, df As Number) As Number
    If t >= 0 Then
        1 - BetaI(df / 2, 0.5, df / (df + t * t)) / 2
    Else
        BetaI(df / 2, 0.5, df / (df + t * t)) / 2

Def FCdf(f As Number, d1 As Number, d2 As Number) As Number
    BetaI(d1 / 2, d2 / 2, d1 * f / (d1 * f + d2))

Rem Quantile functions by bisection — these CDFs have no closed-form
Rem inverses. 80 halvings pin the answer far below the CDFs' own
Rem accuracy. NormInv covers (-13, 13) sigma; TInv covers |t| < 500,
Rem enough for any df >= 1 and confidence level taught anywhere.

Def NormInvGo(p As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number, k As Number) As Number
    Let mid = (lo + hi) / 2
    If k = 0 Then
        mid
    Else
        If NormCdf(mid) < p Then
            NormInvGo(p, mid, hi, k - 1)
        Else
            NormInvGo(p, lo, mid, k - 1)

Def NormInv(p As Number) As Number
    If p <= 0 Or p >= 1 Then
        Error("NORMINV: P OUTSIDE (0, 1)")
    Else
        NormInvGo(p, -13, 13, 80)

Def TInvGo(p As Number, df As Number, lo As Number, hi As Number, k As Number) As Number
    Let mid = (lo + hi) / 2
    If k = 0 Then
        mid
    Else
        If TCdf(mid, df) < p Then
            TInvGo(p, df, mid, hi, k - 1)
        Else
            TInvGo(p, df, lo, mid, k - 1)

Def TInv(p As Number, df As Number) As Number
    If p <= 0 Or p >= 1 Then
        Error("TINV: P OUTSIDE (0, 1)")
    Else
        TInvGo(p, df, -500, 500, 80)

Rem ---- inference -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Every test returns a TestResult; PVal is always two-sided.

Type TestResult
    Stat As Number
    Df As Number
    PVal As Number

Rem Two-sided p for a t statistic — the incomplete beta directly.
Def TwoSidedTP(t As Number, df As Number) As Number
    BetaI(df / 2, 0.5, df / (df + t * t))

Rem One-sample t-test of the mean against mu0.
Def TTest1(xs As List Of Number, mu0 As Number) As TestResult
    Let df = Length(xs) - 1
    Let t = (Mean(xs) - mu0) / StdErr(xs)
    TestResult(t, df, TwoSidedTP(t, df))

Rem Pooled variance of two samples — the classic equal-variance form.
Def PooledVar(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Number
    ((Length(xs) - 1) * Var(xs) + (Length(ys) - 1) * Var(ys)) / (Length(xs) + Length(ys) - 2)

Rem Two-sample t-test for independent groups (pooled / equal-variance,
Rem the textbook form: R's t.test(var.equal = TRUE)).
Def TTest2(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As TestResult
    Let df = Length(xs) + Length(ys) - 2
    Let se = Sqr(PooledVar(xs, ys) * (1 / Length(xs) + 1 / Length(ys)))
    Let t = (Mean(xs) - Mean(ys)) / se
    TestResult(t, df, TwoSidedTP(t, df))

Rem Paired t-test: a one-sample test on the before/after differences.
Def TTestPaired(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As TestResult
    TTest1(ZipWith(xs, ys, -), 0)

Rem One-sample z-test of the mean when sigma is known. Df is 0: no
Rem degrees of freedom apply.
Def ZTest1(xs As List Of Number, mu0 As Number, sigma As Number) As TestResult
    Let z = (Mean(xs) - mu0) / (sigma / Sqr(Length(xs)))
    TestResult(z, 0, 2 * (1 - NormCdf(Abs(z))))

Rem One-way ANOVA over 3+ groups. Stat is F; Df is the between-groups
Rem df (groups - 1); the within df is total n - groups.
Def Anova(gs As List Of List Of Number) As TestResult
    Let gm = Mean(Flatten(gs))
    Let k = Length(gs)
    Let n = Length(Flatten(gs))
    Let ssb = Sum(Map(gs, Fn(g) => Length(g) * (Mean(g) - gm) * (Mean(g) - gm)))
    Let f = (ssb / (k - 1)) / (Sum(Map(gs, SqDevSum)) / (n - k))
    TestResult(f, k - 1, 1 - FCdf(f, k - 1, n - k))

Rem One cell's contribution to a chi-square statistic.
Def ChiCell(o As Number, e As Number) As Number
    (o - e) * (o - e) / e

Rem Chi-square goodness of fit: observed vs expected counts.
Def ChiSqGof(obs As List Of Number, exp As List Of Number) As TestResult
    Let x2 = Sum(ZipWith(obs, exp, ChiCell))
    TestResult(x2, Length(obs) - 1, 1 - Chi2Cdf(x2, Length(obs) - 1))

Def ColSums(rows As List Of List Of Number) As List Of Number
    Map(Range(1, Length(First(rows))), Fn(j) => Sum(Map(rows, Fn(r) => Nth(r, j))))

Rem One row's chi-square contribution against its expected counts.
Def RowChi(r As List Of Number, rsum As Number, csums As List Of Number, total As Number) As Number
    Sum(Map(Range(1, Length(csums)), Fn(j) => ChiCell(Nth(r, j), rsum * Nth(csums, j) / total)))

Rem Chi-square test of independence on a contingency table given as a
Rem list of rows; expected counts from the row and column totals.
Def ChiSqTest(rows As List Of List Of Number) As TestResult
    Let csums = ColSums(rows)
    Let total = Sum(Map(rows, Sum))
    Let x2 = Sum(ZipWith(rows, Map(rows, Sum), Fn(r, rs) => RowChi(r, rs, csums, total)))
    Let df = (Length(rows) - 1) * (Length(csums) - 1)
    TestResult(x2, df, 1 - Chi2Cdf(x2, df))

Rem Two-proportion z-test: k1 successes of n1 vs k2 of n2, pooled SE.
Def TwoPropZTest(k1 As Number, n1 As Number, k2 As Number, n2 As Number) As TestResult
    Let pp = (k1 + k2) / (n1 + n2)
    Let z = (k1 / n1 - k2 / n2) / Sqr(pp * (1 - pp) * (1 / n1 + 1 / n2))
    TestResult(z, 0, 2 * (1 - NormCdf(Abs(z))))

Rem ---- confidence intervals and effect sizes ---------------------------

Rem Confidence interval for the mean (t-based): Pair(lo, hi).
Def MeanCI(xs As List Of Number, conf As Number) As Pair
    Let me = TInv(0.5 + conf / 2, Length(xs) - 1) * StdErr(xs)
    Pair(Mean(xs) - me, Mean(xs) + me)

Rem Confidence interval for a proportion (normal approximation / Wald),
Rem k successes out of n: Pair(lo, hi).
Def PropCI(k As Number, n As Number, conf As Number) As Pair
    Let ph = k / n
    Let me = NormInv(0.5 + conf / 2) * Sqr(ph * (1 - ph) / n)
    Pair(ph - me, ph + me)

Rem Cohen's d: standardized difference of two means (pooled SD).
Def CohenD(xs As List Of Number, ys As List Of Number) As Number
    (Mean(xs) - Mean(ys)) / Sqr(PooledVar(xs, ys))
